				<title>
					<p>21</p>
				</title>
				<p>R. F. Baumeister, E. J. Masicampo &amp; C. N. DeWall, 2009. Prosocial benefits of feeling free: Disbelief in free will increases aggression and reduces helpfulness. <emphasis>Personality and Social Psychology Bulletin,</emphasis> 35: 260–268.</p>
			</section>
			<section id="c_22">
				<title>
					<p>22</p>
				</title>
				<p>J. Diamond, 2008. Vengeance in ours. <emphasis>The New Yorker</emphasis>, April 21, 2001, pp. 74–87.</p>
			</section>
